<p>Our <a href="/export-process/">Export Process</a> page is the reference overview: the eleven steps every order passes through. This guide covers what that sequence feels like from the buyer's side on a <em>first</em> order: roughly when each thing happens, what lands in your inbox at each stage, which decisions are yours to make, and where first orders usually slow down. It's written for importers who haven't bought from us before, and especially for those buying from India for the first time.</p>

<h2>What to prepare before your first enquiry</h2>
<p>The fastest first orders start with a specific enquiry. You don't need every answer, but the more of this you have to hand, the fewer rounds of questions before a firm price:</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Prepare</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Product and grade</td><td>Price and availability depend on the exact grade, not the product name</td><td>"1121 basmati, sella, 2% broken max" rather than "basmati rice"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Quantity and frequency</td><td>Sets container type and count, and whether a trial order makes sense</td><td>One 20ft trial, then monthly</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Destination port</td><td>Needed for any CFR/CIF price and for transit time</td><td>Jebel Ali, Chattogram, Santos</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Preferred Incoterm</td><td>Decides who books freight and insurance</td><td>FOB if you have a forwarder, CIF if not</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Packaging and labelling</td><td>Affects cost, container loading and any private-label artwork</td><td>25 kg PP bags, buyer's brand</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Your compliance checklist</td><td>Lists the documents your authorities and customers need</td><td>Phytosanitary, certificate of origin, lab report</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Import permit status</td><td>Some products need a permit before shipping, and sometimes before a sample</td><td>Permit applied for, or not required</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Payment preference</td><td>Lets us quote on terms your bank can support</td><td>LC at sight, or partial advance</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p>The <a href="/get-a-quote/">quote form</a> prompts for most of these. If you're unsure about one, say so; we'd rather ask a question than guess.</p>

